# 6.  #4 -- is the dS (constant-H) pole LEGITIMATELY applied to the FLRW growing mode?
##############################################################################################
        z     H(z)/H_Lambda    background        pole-transplant valid?
        0.0       1.21         Lambda-dom (dS-like)  YES
        0.5       1.60         matter-dom (NOT dS)   NO -- transplant fails
        1.0       2.16         matter-dom (NOT dS)   NO -- transplant fails
        2.0       3.66         matter-dom (NOT dS)   NO -- transplant fails
        3.0       5.52         matter-dom (NOT dS)   NO -- transplant fails
   [PASS] dS pole transplant is background-valid only at z<~0.7 (H(z)/H_Lam<1.5); FAILS in the matter era where most growth accrues
        => #4 ANSWER: the dS-worldline pole is NOT cleanly transferable to the FLRW growing
           mode across cosmic history. It is defensible near z=0 (Lambda-dominated, dS-like),
           NOT at z>~0.7 (matter-dominated). A constant cH_Lam floor over-applied at all z
           (FLOOR_const_allz) is thus NOT derived -- it borrows a late-time dS result for the
           whole history. The rising c*H(z) floor tracks H(z) but then equals cH0*E(z), which
           switches MI off (nu->1) at all z -> LCDM-degenerate. Neither is forced.
